   "source": [
    "Meviews_stoc = Makemodel(eviews_text, type_input='eviews',\n",
    "                         transform=functools.partial(eviews_to_modelflow, behavioral_opts='<stoc>'))\n",
    "Meviews_stoc.show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "e947c2f7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "FRML <STOC> C = (EXP(C_A+ (0.5*LOG(YD)+0.4*LOG(C(-1))+0.1) )) * (1-C_D)+ C_X*C_D  $\n",
      "FRML <> YD = Y-T $\n",
      "FRML <EXO> Y = (C+I+G)* (1-Y_D)+ Y_X*Y_D $\n",
      "\n",
      "FRML <CALC_ADD_FACTOR>  C_A = - ((0.5*LOG(YD)+0.4*LOG(C(-1))+0.1)) +LOG(C) $\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "Mgekko_exo = Makemodel(gekko_text, type_input='gekko',\n",
    "                       transform=functools.partial(gekko_to_modelflow, code_map={'_GJR': '<exo>'}))\n",
    "Mgekko_exo.show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2f1fa06f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A transformation function of your own can also build on a preset one -- do your own translations\n",
    "first, then hand the equation on:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "80decbcd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "FRML <STOC> C = (EXP(C_A+ (0.5*LOG(YD)+0.4*LOG(C(-1))+0.1) )) * (1-C_D)+ C_X*C_D  $\n",
      "FRML <> YD = Y-T $\n",
      "FRML <ADD> Y = (C+I+G + Y_A)                                $\n",
      "\n",
      "FRML <CALC_ADD_FACTOR>  C_A = - ((0.5*LOG(YD)+0.4*LOG(C(-1))+0.1)) +LOG(C) $ \n",
      "FRML <CALC_ADD_FACTOR>  Y_A = (Y) - (C+I+G) $\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def my_gekko(stmt):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Gekko, with the variable name YD written as YDISP in the source\"\"\"\n",
    "    return gekko_to_modelflow(re.sub(r'\\bydisp\\b', 'yd', stmt, flags=re.IGNORECASE))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Makemodel(gekko_text.replace('yd', 'ydisp'), type_input='gekko', transform=my_gekko).show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1dec3d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Quick reference\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "Makemodel(text)                                   # Markdown: equations on lines starting with >\n",
    "Makemodel(text, type_input='modelflow')           # plain ModelFlow, with or without FRML ... $\n",
    "Makemodel(text, type_input='gekko')               # Gekko FRML ... $ with codes\n",
    "Makemodel(text, type_input='eviews')              # EViews, one equation per line\n",
    "Makemodel(text, eq_start='EQUATION', eq_end='END',\n",
    "          comment_start='#', transform=my_transform)   # a format of your own\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "| What you need | How |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Equations spanning several lines | `eq_end=` |\n",
    "| Ignore text between equations | `eq_start=` |\n",
    "| Comments | `comment_start=` |\n",
    "| Several markers | a list, e.g. `eq_end=['$', ';']` |\n",
    "| Translate or tag each equation | `transform=`, a function `str -> str` |\n",
    "| Drop a statement | let `transform` return `None` |\n",
    "| Change a preset | pass the argument, the rest of the preset is kept |\n",
    "| Options of a preset function | `functools.partial(gekko_to_modelflow, code_map=...)` |\n",
    "| Lists | `list_defs=`, Markdown for Markdown input, plain text otherwise |\n",
    "| See what was extracted | `extract_equations(text, start=..., end=..., comment=..., transform=...)` |"
   ]
  },
